# Keep generated secrets + HA runtime state OUT of git. Only the committed
# prod skeleton (configuration.yaml, *.template) is tracked.
secrets.yaml

# ── The home's own automations, scripts and scenes ────────────────────────────
# These are CUSTOMER STATE, not code. They were tracked and shipped as empty
# `[]` placeholders, which meant every release checkout overwrote a live home's
# real automations and a backup/restore dance was the only thing putting them
# back. On 2026-08-14 that dance restored an EMPTY copy over a good one and the
# Canary ran five and a half hours with zero automations — Leave Home, Pre-cool
# and every Smart Room rule dead — with nothing reporting it.
#
# Ignoring them fixes three things at once:
#   1. a checkout can no longer touch them, so nothing needs to restore them;
#   2. the tree stops being permanently dirty, which ended the auto-stash loop
#      that had accumulated 2331 stashes at one every two minutes; and
#   3. `git stash push -u` stops sweeping untracked files next to them — that is
#      how the FCM push credential silently vanished on 2026-08-10.
#
# configuration.yaml stays tracked: it is Ziggy's skeleton, not the user's, and
# it must be updatable by release. HA `!include`s the three files below, so the
# updater seeds an empty one when missing (see ensure_ha_state_files).
automations.yaml
scripts.yaml
scenes.yaml
.storage/
.cloud/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log
*.log.*
home-assistant.log.fault
tts/
deps/
.HA_VERSION
.ha_run.lock
__pycache__/
